<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bogislaw X</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1454–1523</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Bogislaw X, Duke of Pomerania, Bogislaw the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bogislaw X was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> from 1474, called the Great. By 1478 he had reunited all the divided Pomeranian duchies under his rule. He reformed the administration and finances, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Stettin</a> his main residence and resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>'s claims to overlordship, which were largely settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pyritz">Treaty of Pyritz</a> in 1493.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bogislaw-x.jpg" alt="Bogislaw X" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unbekannter Meister · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bogislaw_X_von_Pommern.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
